            <ArticleTitle>[Painless ST elevation with syncope. Diagnosis by continuous electrocardiography].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>993-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aetiology of syncope in a 53 year old man was discovered on continuous ambulatory electrocardiography. A ventricular arrhythmia associated with ST elevation was recorded. It proved resistant to medical therapy and a double aorto-coronary bypass graft was performed. Post-operative Holter monitoring showed surgery to have been effective.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
